#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0077B expect=violation domain=ADSL
#note "trt01p / trt01pn spelled in lower case. Column names match case-insensitively on every surface (owner ruling 2026-09-28), so the lowercase spelling a SAS dataset may carry satisfies the Requirements.Variables.All templates and the rule executes with the same verdict as on the uppercase twin (PMDA-AD0077B-invalid_two_labels_for_one_code): code 0 carries both PLACEBO and PLCB, PLACEBO is the strict majority, so row 3 alone fires (PMDA-AD0077B: TRTxxP must hold one value per TRTxxPN)."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=3 USUBJID=003
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col trt01p type=Char
col trt01pn type=Num
---
S1 | 001 | PLACEBO | 0
S1 | 002 | PLACEBO | 0
S1 | 003 | PLCB | 0
S1 | 004 | DRUGA | 1
S1 | 005 | DRUGA | 1
